</ul><h1>Not Spicy, But Also Spicy</h1><p>On a recent sale, <a href="/@goldnectar">@goldnectar</a> made a simple, straightforward demand:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Gimme some cheap snacks</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well, goldnectar, we’ll do you one better. Not cheap snacks, but rather, cheap MEALS!</p>
<p>What we have here are some creamy mushroom pasta bowls from everyone’s favorite producer of abusively spicy ramen. Not only are they high in protein and easy to make; they’re also feats of science. After all, how else are they able to get so much flavor out of a single ingredient?</p>
<p>According to the Amazon page:</p>
<p><img height="154" src="https://d2b8wt72ktn9a2.cloudfront.net/mediocre/image/upload/v1775166705/pebi850zdvvqy3ytv8tk.png" width="282" /></p>
<p>That’s right! Each bowl has apparently been extracted from a single garbanzo bean!</p>
<p>Or does it go deeper than that? Is the entire <em>stock</em> of these bowls the product of some ungodly thing done to one chick pea somewhere out there??</p>
<p>Okay, obviously we’re joking. There are other ingredients. And you can see what they are by reading the nutritional information.</p>
<p>The bigger question is, do all those ingredients, you know, taste good?</p>
<p>Here’s what we learned from reading a few Amazon reviews.</p>
<p>Frances likes it:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This looks and tastes amazing. The sauce is thick and creamy.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>shelley a. also likes it:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This is so yummy! I love mushrooms and the flavor is so rich. Not too much, but just right.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>jenny maybe likes it a bit too much:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This is by far the best pasta I’ve eaten, and I mean it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Seriously, jenny, if you’re happy, we’re happy, but you might need to get out more.</p>
<p>Nitasha McCluskey likes it as well and gives the most detailed review:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hands down, one of the best cups of noodles I’ve ever had. All the others are really spicy. I LOVE spicy food. But sometimes it’s nice to just have a creamy bowl of noodles that’s not spicy. I amp up the creaminess by always adding a splash of heavy cream at the very end when it’s done microwaving and time to pour the “powder pack” inside and give it a good mix. Although it’s not spicy, it’s extremely flavorful.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Here, we get a direct statement of what the other reviews only implied: despite being from Samyang, this pasta <strong>isn’t spicy</strong>.</p>
<p>Which might be a selling point for some, but not for others. So we figured, why not do a little something for everyone? Hence why we’re also including two bottles of the Samyang Buldak Carbonara Hot Sauce. It’ll pack a nice bit of heat and taste great drizzled over your mushroom bowls (or anything else). And since it’s a bottle, you wimps who enjoy a bit of heat but not too much can add as little as you want!</p>
<p>(I’m talking to myself here, in case that wasn’t clear.)</p>
<p>Bon appetite, down the hatch.</p>